OL,3,GNEWSAWhat a lower tax rise could mean
OL,4,Afor you - and the council
OL,5,
OL,6,FAutumn can be a busy time for those of
OL,7,Fus who keep a close eye on politics, as
OL,8,Fcouncils across the country start
OL,9,Fsetting out their financial plans for
OL,10,Fthe year ahead.
OL,12,FCouncil tax is set every year by local
OL,13,Fauthorities to raise money for things
OL,14,Flike rubbish collection, street
OL,15,Flighting, parks and libraries.
OL,17,FI have covered local councils and their
OL,18,Fbudgets for more than a decade, and
OL,19,Fover that time it has become almost
OL,20,Fexpected that our bills will rise by
OL,21,F4.99% each year - with 2% of that
OL,22,Fprotected for adult social care.
OL,23,APub: 10-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
